<task id="022" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Build cross-tenant CIAM Graph client (app-only)</title>
    <phase>2 Identity + provisioning + document content</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <status-note>2026-07-19 COMPLETE. New `Infrastructure/Graph/CiamGraphClientFactory.cs` (concrete sealed singleton, no interface per ADR-010 — mirrors SpeAdminTokenProvider). App-only client-credentials against the CIAM authority ({Ciam:Instance}/{Ciam:TenantId}) via a cached per-authority MSAL ConfidentialClientApplication built WithCertificate + WithAuthority; AcquireTokenForClient(["graph/.default"]) — NO OBO, NO UserAssertion (broker-only, ADR-028 A1). Cert loaded at runtime from Key Vault via the shared SecretClient (KV cert PFX exposed as same-named secret; exportable RSA-2048 confirmed via az); EphemeralKeySet (in-memory, never on disk); only the non-secret cert NAME + provisioner clientId placeholders live in config (NFR-06). Exposes AcquireAppOnlyTokenAsync (token seam) + CreateClientForAppAsync (GraphServiceClient v1.0 over the resilient "GraphApiClient" HttpClient). Registered `services.AddSingleton<CiamGraphClientFactory>()` in ExternalAccessModule. Config: added Ciam:GraphProvisioner {ClientId, CertificateName} sub-section to appsettings.template.json (#{CIAM_GRAPH_PROVISIONER_APP_ID}# / #{CIAM_GRAPH_PROVISIONER_CERT_NAME}#) + comment. Build 0 errors; publish 45.69 MB compressed (≤60); no new packages; no new HIGH CVE. code-review + adr-check clean. Runtime prereq for task 031: BFF MI needs KV 'Secrets User' on spaarke-spekvcert to read the cert PFX. Consumed by task 025 (provisioner).</status-note>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New cross-tenant auth component reaching a second tenant's Graph (tags: auth)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New cross-tenant auth component (tags: auth)</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-safe-reason>new Graph client + DI wiring</parallel-safe-reason>
    <deps>002</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 dev-day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build an app-only Microsoft Graph client that targets the Entra External ID (CIAM) tenant, modeled on `SpeAdmin/SpeAdminTokenProvider.GetOrCreateMsalApp` (per-authority `WithAuthority`, credential from Key Vault secret or Managed-Identity-as-Federated-Identity-Credential). The existing `GraphClientFactory` is single-tenant and cannot target the CIAM tenant. Register the new client in DI. No plaintext secrets.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    You are a BFF identity engineer building a cross-tenant app-only Graph client for CIAM user management, reusing the established per-authority MSAL app pattern from SpeAdmin.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new app-only Graph client (under `Infrastructure/Graph/` or `Services/`) acquires an application token for the CIAM tenant via a per-authority MSAL app modeled on `SpeAdminTokenProvider.GetOrCreateMsalApp` (`WithAuthority(ciamAuthority)`), with the client credential sourced from Key Vault (cert) or MI-as-FIC; it is registered in DI and usable by the provisioner (task 025). No plaintext secret is used.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The BFF must create/manage users in the CIAM tenant (Graph `POST /users`), which requires an app-only Graph token issued by the CIAM tenant's own app registration (task 002). `GraphClientFactory.ForApp()` is single-tenant (workforce) and has no authority parameter, so it cannot reach the CIAM tenant. `SpeAdminTokenProvider.GetOrCreateMsalApp` already implements the cross-tenant/per-authority MSAL confidential-client pattern (per-customer authority + KV secret) — this task models the CIAM client on it. Credential path (cert-in-KV vs MI-as-FIC) is decided in task 002; this task consumes that decision.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/SpeAdmin/SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/GraphClientFactory.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: external-surface outbound. The CIAM Graph client is app-only (application permissions in the CIAM tenant) — the external user's token is NEVER exchanged; broker-only invariant (Amendment A1). No OBO.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">Scope: the CIAM app credential. Store the credential in Key Vault (cert) or eliminate via MI-as-FIC — NO plaintext secret in source or config; reference via `@Microsoft.KeyVault(...)` in production.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Scope: Graph client construction. Follow the established per-authority MSAL confidential-client pattern from `SpeAdminTokenProvider.GetOrCreateMsalApp` (WithAuthority per authority); do not fork a divergent auth mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. Register the client as a concrete/interface pair per DI minimalism; do not over-abstract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this BFF task. State the §10 BFF Hygiene Placement Justification in the PR description (cite `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`), and report BFF compressed publish size + diff vs baseline (~49.63 MB) confirming the ≤60 MB ceiling (NFR-01).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <justification>
    <existing>`GraphClientFactory` is single-tenant (no authority parameter); `SpeAdminTokenProvider.GetOrCreateMsalApp` is the cross-tenant per-authority template.</existing>
    <extension>No — `GraphClientFactory` cannot target the CIAM tenant; model a new client on `SpeAdminTokenProvider` instead.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a cross-tenant CIAM Graph client, the BFF cannot create or manage CIAM users (the app permission lives in the CIAM tenant) — admin-initiated onboarding cannot mint a credential.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/SpeAdmin/SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs</file>
      <file>.claude/agent-memory/researcher/ciam-user-provisioning-graph-2026-07-19.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read `SpeAdminTokenProvider.GetOrCreateMsalApp` to learn the per-authority MSAL confidential-client construction (WithAuthority + KV-backed credential caching).</step>
    <step>Read task 002's recorded credential decision (cert-in-KV vs MI-as-FIC) and the CIAM app-reg identifiers from `config/environments.json`.</step>
    <step>Implement a CIAM Graph client that builds a per-authority MSAL app against the CIAM authority and acquires an app-only Graph token (`.default`), exposing a `GraphServiceClient` (or equivalent) for user operations.</step>
    <step>Register the client in DI (concrete + minimal interface) so the provisioner can consume it.</step>
    <step>Build and run `dotnet publish -c Release`; record compressed size + diff vs the ~49.63 MB baseline.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If Managed-Identity-as-Federated-Identity-Credential (MI-as-FIC) is not GA/available at build time, fall back to a certificate stored in Key Vault per task 002; if neither credential path is available, STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 rather than embedding a plaintext secret.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output>A cross-tenant app-only CIAM Graph client under Infrastructure/Graph/ or Services/, registered in DI.</output>
    <output>Credential sourced from Key Vault / MI-as-FIC (no plaintext).</output>
    <output>BFF publish-size report (compressed size + diff).</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The client acquires an app-only Graph token for the CIAM tenant (per-authority MSAL app against the CIAM authority).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The credential is sourced from Key Vault or MI-as-FIC; negative: no plaintext secret appears in source or config.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The client is registered in DI and resolvable for CIAM user operations.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the client does not perform any OBO/user-token exchange (app-only only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF compressed publish size is reported with diff and stays ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on task 002 (CIAM app registration + credential decision). Consumed by task 025 (provisioner). Models the cross-tenant pattern on SpeAdminTokenProvider rather than extending single-tenant GraphClientFactory.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
